xnu 0176: let CoreAnimation render a smaller canvas and scale it in swap

The CPU rasterizer is the UI wall (9-11 fps at 1440x3200). A boot-arg pair,
mondrianfb_canvas_w/h, makes the default surface and the advertised canvas
smaller than the panel (default: the panel, so a normal boot is unchanged);
swap() then scales a full canvas-sized layer to the panel with a nearest
neighbour pass, which stays in the few-ms budget. The panel timing and the
scanout stay at 1440x3200; the provider carries canvas-width/canvas-height
and GetDisplaySize returns the canvas. The 900x2000 boot accepts the canvas
(AppleCLCD panel 1440x3200 canvas 900x2000); its swap/fps measurement was
cut short by a forced HFS fsck, so the UI gain is still to be measured with
mondrianfb_fps=1.

